WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:16.118
"A thief at the barn?"

2
00:00:16.478 --> 00:00:17.118
Henry said.

3
00:00:17.139 --> 00:00:20.240
"What are you talking about, Maggie?"

4
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.042
By now Maggie's father, Henry's uncle Bruce, had come into the backyard.

5
00:00:25.062 --> 00:00:29.524
"There's no need to be so dramatic, Maggie," he said with a sigh.

6
00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:32.630
"Mom and I have talked to you before about this.

7
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.732
You need to be more careful with your things."

8
00:00:35.752 --> 00:00:38.914
"But I was being careful!"

9
00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:40.195
Maggie exclaimed.

10
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:44.879
"I left the check on my bag, right on top of my sandals.

11
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.482
It was definitely there when I led my pony outside for our lesson.

12
00:00:50.463 --> 00:00:53.125
But when I got back, the check was gone!"

13
00:00:53.145 --> 00:00:56.368
"Wait a minute," Aunt Ellen said.

14
00:00:57.568 --> 00:01:00.709
"Are you saying you lost the check we wrote for today's lesson?"

15
00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:05.390
"Don't worry, I wrote another one," Uncle Bruce told his wife.

16
00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.631
"And I called the bank to cancel the first check."

17
00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:10.592
"Oh, Maggie."

18
00:01:11.932 --> 00:01:13.072
Aunt Ellen shook her head.

19
00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:18.674
"I can't believe you were so careless, especially after what happened last week."

20
00:01:19.694 --> 00:01:20.894
Henry was surprised.

21
00:01:22.035 --> 00:01:24.055
Maggie could be careless about some things.

22
00:01:25.115 --> 00:01:27.116
But she was really careful with her money.

23
00:01:28.748 --> 00:01:30.010
"What happened last week?"

24
00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.031
he asked.

25
00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:35.255
"Maggie lost a few other things at the barn," Uncle Bruce said.

26
00:01:35.275 --> 00:01:38.719
"Oh dear," Henry's mother said.

27
00:01:38.739 --> 00:01:41.862
"I didn't lose anything!"

28
00:01:42.282 --> 00:01:43.304
Maggie protested.

29
00:01:43.324 --> 00:01:46.147
"Someone has been stealing things!"

30
00:01:47.448 --> 00:01:50.111
"Really? What else disappeared?"

31
00:01:50.471 --> 00:01:51.252
Henry asked.

32
00:01:52.784 --> 00:01:58.349
"At my first lesson, I took off my charm bracelet and left it in the barn," Maggie said.

33
00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:01.492
"I didn't want to lose it while I was riding.

34
00:02:02.653 --> 00:02:06.476
When I came back inside after my lesson, it was gone!"

35
00:02:06.496 --> 00:02:11.360
"I don't know why you were so worried about losing it," her mother said.

36
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:16.024
"You always let those kittens of yours use it as a cat toy!"

37
00:02:17.385 --> 00:02:18.266
Maggie frowned.

38
00:02:18.286 --> 00:02:20.268
"That's different.

39
00:02:21.324 --> 00:02:23.065
The kittens just bat it around.

40
00:02:24.205 --> 00:02:25.506
I always know where it is."

41
00:02:25.526 --> 00:02:28.727
"Did anything else disappear?"

42
00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:29.828
Henry asked.

43
00:02:30.848 --> 00:02:32.809
He was already thinking like a detective.

44
00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.791
The first thing a good detective needed to do was find out the facts of the case.

45
00:02:39.612 --> 00:02:40.292
Maggie nodded.

46
00:02:40.312 --> 00:02:46.135
"At my second lesson, my brand-new horse grooming brush disappeared," she said.

47
00:02:46.155 --> 00:02:48.556
"It happened the same way.

48
00:02:49.672 --> 00:02:54.275
It was in the barn when I went outside for my lesson, but gone when I got back."

49
00:02:54.295 --> 00:02:57.858
"Don't forget about your gloves," her father said.

50
00:02:57.878 --> 00:03:01.120
"Oh, right," Maggie said.

51
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.943
"I didn't wear my riding gloves today because it was so hot.

52
00:03:06.143 --> 00:03:07.965
I left them with my stuff in the barn.

53
00:03:09.025 --> 00:03:11.427
Whoever took that check must have taken the gloves too."

54
00:03:11.447 --> 00:03:15.610
"Maggie!" Aunt Ellen looked shocked.

55
00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.592
"Those gloves were expensive!"

56
00:03:20.324 --> 00:03:23.827
"Everything about horseback riding is expensive," Uncle Bruce agreed.

57
00:03:23.847 --> 00:03:26.730
"We can't afford to keep replacing things."

58
00:03:27.891 --> 00:03:31.354
Henry could tell that Maggie's parents thought she'd lost all those things.

59
00:03:32.435 --> 00:03:33.716
But he wasn't so sure.

60
00:03:34.737 --> 00:03:37.559
Maggie was too careful with money to misplace a check.

61
00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.444
She was so excited about riding that he couldn't believe she'd lose a horse brush or her riding

62
00:03:43.484 --> 00:03:47.568
gloves. And he knew she loved that charm bracelet.

63
00:03:48.576 --> 00:03:52.300
"Is anyone allowed inside the barn while there's a lesson outside?"

64
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.641
he asked Maggie.

65
00:03:53.661 --> 00:03:57.824
"Sure, I guess so," Maggie said with a shrug.

66
00:03:57.844 --> 00:04:01.047
"I mean, they don't close the doors or anything.

67
00:04:02.088 --> 00:04:04.130
Any rotten thief could just walk in."

68
00:04:06.071 --> 00:04:07.212
She clenched her fists.

69
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:10.836
"I can't believe someone is doing this to me!"

70
00:04:12.417 --> 00:04:15.560
She sounded so dramatic again that all the adults looked at each other.

71
00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.162
But Maggie's words made Henry think of another question.

72
00:04:19.182 --> 00:04:21.744
"Has anything else disappeared?"

73
00:04:22.105 --> 00:04:22.825
he asked her.

74
00:04:22.845 --> 00:04:26.448
"I mean, anything belonging to other people.

75
00:04:27.529 --> 00:04:28.910
Or is it only your stuff?"

76
00:04:29.931 --> 00:04:30.892
"How should I know?"

77
00:04:31.353 --> 00:04:32.053
Maggie frowned.

78
00:04:32.073 --> 00:04:35.136
"That's what I need you to find out!

79
00:04:36.257 --> 00:04:38.919
Dad made me leave the barn before I could investigate."

80
00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.161
Uncle Bruce shook his head.

81
00:04:41.181 --> 00:04:44.744
"We were already late for this barbecue," he said.

82
00:04:45.804 --> 00:04:47.906
"Besides, I don't think there's a mystery here.

83
00:04:48.986 --> 00:04:51.368
It just means that you have to be more careful with your things."

84
00:04:51.388 --> 00:04:54.851
"That's right," Aunt Ellen said.

85
00:04:54.871 --> 00:05:00.455
"I had to pull your favorite horse T-shirt out from under your desk this morning.

86
00:05:01.396 --> 00:05:03.137
The kittens were using it as a bed.

87
00:05:04.618 --> 00:05:07.120
It was absolutely covered in cat hair."

88
00:05:07.921 --> 00:05:09.342
Henry's mother cleared her throat.

89
00:05:09.362 --> 00:05:12.004
"Should we eat?

90
00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.742
Everything smells delicious, and I'm hungry," she said.

91
00:05:16.762 --> 00:05:20.424
"Good idea, Susan," Uncle Bruce agreed.

92
00:05:20.444 --> 00:05:23.285
"Go sit down at the picnic table, everybody.

93
00:05:24.405 --> 00:05:26.266
I'll help Kevin bring the food over from the grill."

94
00:05:27.287 --> 00:05:29.888
The adults were obviously ready to change the subject.

95
00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:37.692
But later, while everyone was eating, Maggie was still thinking about her missing things.

96
00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.581
"I didn't lose my stuff at the barn!"

97
00:05:43.001 --> 00:05:43.841
she said loudly.

98
00:05:43.861 --> 00:05:46.422
"Somebody stole it!

99
00:05:47.543 --> 00:05:50.264
And The Lemonade Detectives will figure out who it was!"

100
00:05:51.544 --> 00:05:53.625
Aunt Ellen glanced up from her corn on the cob.

101
00:05:53.645 --> 00:05:56.726
"I hope so, Maggie," she said.

102
00:05:56.746 --> 00:06:01.788
"Because if this keeps happening, you might not be able to keep riding."
